    {
      "id": "claim_ab78ccc61fe94957bb7dd3b553378b73",
      "statement": "The /pet on|off|toggle command is a client inputTriggers source on the '/' trigger registered after the built-in dsh command source, so adjudicate's first-non-undefined (registration-ordered) polling lets it take over /pet for unknown commands. matchEnter matches /^\\/pet(?:\\s+(on|off|toggle))?$/i, calls the petStore show/hide/toggle (defaulting to toggle), consumes the line via slash/input-consume-token with a bare-token guard, and returns 'handled' so the line is never sent to the model. onPick consumes the input with a span guard. Consumption failures are caught and ignored without rolling back the pet state change.",
